experiment: objname
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 900000. derived: g3probe's session again, so g3probe's budget -- 141 probes per
  creature. §50 asks the other half of §49: the index is the INPUT to the
  per-context bias table, and whether the VOICE then learns a per-object
  bias off it is a separate question. No new mechanism -- bias_ctx_ is
  already learned by node perturbation keyed on active_ctx_, so §49's arms
  ran this table and visprobe never scored it. 12 creatures, not 5:
  ctxsrc read 0.754 at 3 and PRINTED A LICENCE, then 0.740 at 9 and
  refused. Four arms on ONE code path differing only in index CONTENT --
  BASE (table off), RET (derived off the retina), ORACLE (pinned to the
  true object) and SHUF (pinned to a drawn one). ORACLE is the ceiling
  without which a RET null cannot separate 'the index is too weak' from
  'the table cannot express an object-specific voice at all'; SHUF is the
  label-destroyed control without which an effect could be mere dropout.
  kRead because every branch prints a reading rather than returning false
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §50. §49 showed the creature can DERIVE a visual index
                    (ctx_match 0.8624 vs null 0.5346). Does the VOICE then
                    learn a per-object bias off it -- does it speak the
                    object it sees?
  the mechanism     bias_ctx_[i * slots + active_ctx_], learned by node
                    perturbation and read back into the drive. Already in
                    the kernel; §49's arms ran it and never scored it.
  the prediction    ctxsrc named PERSISTENCE as what stands between areax
                    v51 and naming: the word is at 1.000 while it plays and
                    0.533 by the reward window. AN OBJECT IN VIEW DOES NOT
                    STOP, so that obstruction should not arise. Clause 3
                    MEASURES that rather than asserting it.
  session           150.0 s x 12 creatures x 4 index arms x 2 target arms
  instrument        objname   trial seed 0000000001357778   12 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 1 -- IS THE INDEX LIVE, AND IS IT BALANCED? §49's first smoke read
  ctx_match exactly 0.5000 against a null of exactly 0.5000 because the
  partition had COLLAPSED onto one slice, and ctx_present_frac read 1.0000
  throughout -- a constant index is perfectly live. Occupancy is the share
  of probes in the busiest slice: 0.500 balanced, 1.000 collapsed.
    BASE    creatures 12/12  ctx_slots 0 (asked 0)  present 0.0000  occupancy 0.0000  <- table OFF by design
    RET     creatures 12/12  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.8917  
    ORACLE  creatures 12/12  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5000  
    SHUF    creatures 12/12  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5958  

  CLAUSE 2 -- DOES §49 REPRODUCE HERE? A different instrument invocation is
  exactly where this project has found harness divergence before, so the
  index is re-measured rather than cited. §49 read RET at +0.3278.
    arm     ctx_match  null       excess     window
    RET     0.5333     0.5549     -0.0216    probes
    ORACLE  1.0000     0.5807     +0.4193    probes
    SHUF    0.6375     0.5896     +0.0479    probes

  *** REFUSED, PRE-REGISTERED: RET excess -0.0216 is under the +0.15 bar, so
  §50 is NOT running on the index §49 found and nothing below is
  interpretable as a test of it.

  CLAUSE 3 -- IS THE INDEX THERE WHEN THE MECHANISM NEEDS IT? ctxsrc's rule:
  'before wiring a signal into a mechanism, check it is still there WHEN THE
  MECHANISM NEEDS IT' -- coderprobe's 0.981 and ctxsrc's 0.533 are the same
  module 400 ms apart. The bias table is written where REWARD lands, so the
  teaching window is the one that matters, not the probe.
    arm     window       ctx_match  null       excess
    RET     probe        0.5333     0.5549     -0.0216
            TEACHING     0.5505     0.5543     -0.0038
    ORACLE  probe        1.0000     0.5807     +0.4193
            TEACHING     1.0000     0.5553     +0.4447
    SHUF    probe        0.6375     0.5896     +0.0479
            TEACHING     0.5533     0.5514     +0.0019

    RET: probe -0.0216, teaching -0.0038. A teaching value well below the
    probe value is the AUDITORY failure reappearing in the visual path --
    an index that is right when looked at and gone when used.

  CLAUSE 4 -- THE VOICE. Two estimators, and the ORDER MATTERS.

  4a (PRIMARY) -- THE TAUGHT DIRECTION. Projection of the per-object voice
  difference onto the teacher's axis, in multiples of the separation asked
  for (1.0 = full compliance). Zero expectation under drift, and signed.
    arm     taught             random             taught-random      beat ctl / t>0
    BASE    +0.0314 +- 0.0365  -0.0514 +- 0.0497  +0.0827 +- 0.0561   9/12   8/12
    RET     +0.0583 +- 0.0306  +0.0280 +- 0.0360  +0.0303 +- 0.0502   8/12   8/12
    ORACLE  +0.3966 +- 0.2324  -0.0763 +- 0.1805  +0.4729 +- 0.1393  10/12   8/12
    SHUF    -0.0606 +- 0.0597  -0.0026 +- 0.0510  -0.0580 +- 0.0472   4/12   6/12

  4a PER CREATURE (taught), so the shape of the distribution is visible
  rather than inferred from a mean and an SE:
    BASE    +0.092 -0.098 +0.038 -0.159 +0.095 +0.155 -0.095 +0.074 +0.275 +0.060 -0.114 +0.054
    RET     +0.009 +0.051 -0.014 +0.064 -0.052 +0.273 -0.065 +0.152 +0.155 +0.024 +0.159 -0.057
    ORACLE  +0.696 -0.042 -0.935 +0.465 +1.011 -0.294 +0.574 +1.678 +0.217 +1.242 -0.818 +0.964
    SHUF    +0.169 -0.332 -0.034 -0.394 -0.117 +0.155 -0.196 +0.030 +0.128 +0.129 -0.324 +0.059

  4b (SECONDARY) -- DECODABILITY. Held-out accuracy on object identity.
  CONFOUNDED by table divergence wherever the index is object-correlated,
  so it is reported and NOT used for the verdict. A high number here with a
  zero in 4a means the two voices DIFFER without differing as taught.
    arm     taught           random           taught-random      beat own ctl
    BASE     0.567 +- 0.028   0.517 +- 0.047  +0.050 +- 0.061    5 of 12
    RET      0.483 +- 0.037   0.583 +- 0.032  -0.100 +- 0.049    2 of 12
    ORACLE   0.900 +- 0.046   0.875 +- 0.041  +0.025 +- 0.046    3 of 12
    SHUF     0.533 +- 0.036   0.600 +- 0.035  -0.067 +- 0.038    3 of 12

  CLAUSE 5 -- THE VERDICT, spanning the sign. Paired by creature.
    RET - SHUF     +0.0883  (paired SE 0.0500, so 1.8 SE; unpaired SE 0.0689)
    ORACLE - SHUF  +0.5309  (paired SE 0.1419)
    in these units 1.0 is FULL compliance with the teacher, so 2 SE = 0.1000
    is the smallest share of the asked-for gesture this run can resolve.

    VOID: clause 1 or clause 2 refused above, so the voice table is not a
    test of the visual index. The refusal is the result.
